Z||000000||GT Bastard||12-30-2000||08:20 AM||||I bought another 4cyl Fiero!  I was actually trying to look into an '89 turbo Daytona, but the owner backed-out on me.  It's a white '85 coupe with a 5sp(of course) and 80,000 origional miles.  Body and interior are nice! Engine bay is really clean and she runs real smooth and quiet.  It's got a very recent clutch(it was a friends car) and a few other goodies.  It's got a sunroof and NO options otherwise.  She's gotta be light!  I paid 1,000 bucks for it.  It was either, bum rides everywhere while my SE is down for the engine swap or put off the swap a few weeks and get another car to drive(I just sold my old Mercedes.) Maybe this way it'll be more of a challenge to waste riceboys around town.  I wanna thrown some springs and KYB's on it and autocross it occasion this summer.  Or maybe I can find a cheap nitrous kit and blow it up!   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif">||||reg||1
Z||000001||82-T/A||12-30-2000||09:39 AM||||4 cyl Fieros are fun. I say use it for your daily driver.. IE: Don't spend any money on MODS.. until you get your project car done.<P>Then when your project car is all set.. make that 4 cyl an auto-x car.. or just keep it stock and cruise around in it.<P>You can get some pretty decent performance out of the 4 cyl with a rebuild.<P>Crane roller cam, roller rockers... hooker header.. for under $600 bucks in parts, you can get the 4 cyl close to the stock V6's power. Which really is pretty good considering.<P><P>------------------<BR>Todd Jaspers<BR>1997 Pontiac GrandAm SE<BR>1987 Pontiac Fiero SE/V6<BR>1984 Pontiac Fiero 2m4 SE<BR>http://www.ezshots.com/album.cgi?82tafiero/Apartment||||reg||1
Z||000002||Philphine||12-30-2000||10:46 AM||||make it a "cheap thrills" car like my '84. let it get "hand me downs" from your main fiero if they're improvements. cheap wheels from auto trader or ebay. stuff like that. it's kind of fun to impress people with a car that you've only got a few dollars in. ||||reg||1
Z||000003||Coconut||12-30-2000||12:42 PM||||GTB,  <BR>I'd say you are showing the symptoms of the classically(sp) "TRUE FIERO FANATIC".. seems like us guys do 'em like Lays potato chips...you can't have just one!  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"> LOL!! <P>Believe me, if I had the funds, I know for sure that I would have, at the very minimum, 3 of those puppies! Of course then I'd have to worry about where the hell to keep 'em all.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">  I think that 4 banger would make for a good everyday commuter car. Save money on gas, then use the money you've saved, on more goodies for the SE.<P>Cruisin'  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P>------------------<BR>    <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/Coconut's_Signature_1.JPG">  <p>[This message has been edited by Coconut (edited 12-30-2000).]||||reg||14
